q 0.720 0.720 0.720 RG 0.55 w 50 470.69999999999965 m 562 470.69999999999965 l S Q
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 457.69999999999965 Tm (A reported failure was that enabling modules 5 and 6 \(Loudness and Tone\) could stop speaker) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 444.19999999999965 Tm (output. The project notes identify a root cause in the AGC rolling RMS sum: floating-point) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 430.69999999999965 Tm (subtraction can leave a tiny negative value even though the mathematical sum of squares cannot be) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 417.19999999999965 Tm (negative. Taking sqrt of that negative residue creates NaN; the non-finite gain then contaminates) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 403.69999999999965 Tm (AGC output and the downstream Tone stage, yielding silence. The AGC accumulator is now clamped to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 390.19999999999965 Tm (zero before RMS calculation. The VAD rolling RMS accumulator received the same numerical guard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 371.69999999999965 Tm (- This fix addresses a numeric invalid-state path; it is not an audio level threshold or a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 358.49999999999966 Tm (  substitute for listening tests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 343.29999999999967 Tm (- Synthetic tests were used to verify the dry/DSP routes and Loudness/Tone recovery after) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 330.0999999999997 Tm (  silence. No real microphone was opened during the validation described in the handoff.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 0.040 0.140 0.320 rg 1 0 0 1 50 310.8999999999997 Tm (07  |  De-Reverb artifacts and clipped word endings) Tj ET
q 0.720 0.720 0.720 RG 0.55 w 50 287.8999999999997 m 562 287.8999999999997 l S Q
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 274.8999999999997 Tm (The De-Reverb processor is an envelope shaper, not blind deconvolution or a complete acoustic) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 261.3999999999997 Tm (de-reverberator. Its earlier settings allowed materially faster gain modulation and a wider gain) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 247.8999999999997 Tm (span \(roughly -12 dB attenuation to +3 dB boost, with short symmetric smoothing\). Fast) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 234.3999999999997 Tm (envelope-driven gain changes can sound like pumping/glitches and can reduce the level that reaches) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 220.8999999999997 Tm (the voice detector. The code was made conservative: no boost, a floor near -6 dB, and slower) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.120 rg 1 0 0 1 50 207.3999999999997 Tm (gain-reduction/recovery smoothing of 20/120 ms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 188.8999999999997 Tm (- The VAD is a 32 ms rolling RMS and falling noise-floor/SNR hysteresis detector, not the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 175.6999999999997 Tm (  proposed Otsu classifier. Its enter/exit thresholds are 9/4 dB SNR.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 160.49999999999972 Tm (- Word endings could be classified as inactive after the short original hangover; a second) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 147.29999999999973 Tm (  forced-close timer could override that hold, and the gate could fade down abruptly. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 134.09999999999974 Tm (  forced-close path was removed, VAD hangover increased to 900 ms, gate hold remains an) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 120.89999999999974 Tm (  additional 400 ms and attenuation is ramped over 30 ms.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 105.69999999999973 Tm (- A 0.001 RMS absolute quiet close guard \(~-60 dBFS\) prevents speech from staying latched when) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 92.49999999999973 Tm (  the learned floor becomes extremely low. This fixed threshold is a known tuning risk and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 0.100 0.100 0.100 rg 1 0 0 1 58 79.29999999999973 Tm (  needs representative microphone/noise measurements before changing.) Tj ET
